pve-qemu-anti-detection (1.1.1-1) stable; urgency=high

  * Fix the rebuild hanging indefinitely. The patch was copied into qemu/ and
    so became an untracked file; upstream debian/rules runs "git clean -xdfi"
    on a copy of that tree, and with something to remove the -i makes it print
    "What now>" and wait on stdin forever. The patch is now applied by absolute
    path and never placed inside the source tree.
  * Close stdin for the package build so no interactive prompt can stall it.
  * Restore the apt hold when an upgrade fails or is interrupted. Previously
    "upgrade" unheld the package, installed the stock build over the patched
    one, and left it that way if the rebuild did not finish - the host kept
    running an unpatched qemu with nothing preventing apt from reinstalling it.

 -- Hikaru Chang <i@rua.moe>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 02:45:50 +0900

pve-qemu-anti-detection (1.1.0-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Rebase anti-detection patch onto QEMU 11.0.x
    - hw/pci-host/gpex.c: context changed, set_bit(DEVICE_CATEGORY_BRIDGE)
      was dropped upstream
    - hw/scsi/scsi-bus.c: qemu_hw_version() replaced by the QEMU_HW_VERSION
      macro in trailing context
    - hw/smbios/smbios.c: upstream made the SMBIOS "Virtual Machine" bit
      conditional on smbios_type0.vm; the block is now removed outright so
      the bit is never advertised
  * Add -smbios type=3,chassis-type=N. QEMU hardcodes 0x01 ("Other"), a value
    no real machine reports; the option lets the guest chassis type match the
    host (e.g. 6 = Mini Tower). Defaults to 0x03 (Desktop) when unset.
  * Document full host SMBIOS passthrough (types 0/1/2/3/4/11/17). PVE only
    sets type 1, so the remaining tables fall back to the patch defaults and
    leak "ASUS" into the baseboard, chassis, CPU and memory manufacturers.
  * Correct the claim that OVMF firmware strings cannot be changed: -smbios
    type=0 does override OVMF's own BIOS identity, verified in a guest.

 -- Hikaru Chang <i@rua.moe>  Sun, 13 Sep 2026 20:53:59 +0900

pve-qemu-anti-detection (1.0.1-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Add --cn/--china flag for China mainland mirror mode (GitHub mirrors)
  * Add USE_CN_MIRROR config option for persistent mirror setting
  * Fix KVM CPUID signature: remove kvm.c patch to preserve Linux VM
    paravirtualization (kvm-clock, PV EOI, PV spinlocks, PV IPIs)
  * Update documentation with China mirror instructions and KVM/Windows
    VM configuration guidance

